From 9f5cfd30f0f1851963fae312ece50fac314dc18c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: n0madic <800462+n0madic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:11:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Pace the game by Timer 3 scan lines, PAL rates and host time

The BIOS keeps EE Timer 3 for its alarms, which count scan lines, and
Soulcalibur III paces its main loop on it: after each VSync it busy-waits
until Timer 3 has advanced 311 lines past the VSync stamp. Timer 3 started
at BUSCLK/256, so the wait ended almost at once and the game ran unpaced.

- Timer 3 starts counting H-blanks (CLKS=3), at 15625 Hz once SMODE1
  selects PAL instead of the NTSC 15734 Hz.
- VBlank comes every 20 ms in PAL mode instead of a fixed 60 Hz.
- EE time is an estimate that runs behind real time while the guest spins,
  so a timer count read lets the EE clock catch up with host time since the
  last VBlank, up to the next scheduled event.
